<name><surname>Metz</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>1970</year><article-title>Reduction of incidence of prematurity by folic acid supplementation in pregnancy.</article-title><source>Br Med J</source><volume>1</volume><fpage>16</fpage><lpage>17</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">5460838</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed.1000077-Blot1"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Blot</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Papiernik</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Kaltwasser</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Werner</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Tchernia</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><year>1981</year><article-title>Influence of routine administration of folic acid and iron during pregnancy.</article-title><source>Gynecol Obstet Invest</source><volume>12</volume><fpage>294</fpage><lpage>304</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7297938</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed.1000077-Inskip1"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Inskip</surname><given-names>HM</given-names></name><name><surname>Crozier</surname><given-names>SR</given-names></name><name><surname>Godfrey</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><name><surname>Borland</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name><name><surname>Cooper</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2009</year><article-title>Women's compliance with nutrition and lifestyle recommendations before pregnancy: General population cohort study.</article-title><source>BMJ</source><volume>338</volume><fpage>481</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="pmed.1000077-Centers1"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><collab>Centers for Disease Control and Prevention</collab><year>2008</year><article-title>Trends in wh